                     stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"
                     stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/>
                </svg>
              </button>
            </h3>
            <div class="details">
              <p>Cats have a highly developed "righting reflex" — a sequence of spinal and vestibular movements that lets them orient their body during a fall so their feet point downward. This reflex is fully developed by about 7 weeks of age.</p>
              <p>However, "always" is too strong. Falls from very low heights (under about 60 cm) do not give enough time for the reflex to complete, while falls from very great heights can still cause serious injury. Cats are not immune to fall trauma — never assume a fall is safe.</p>
